---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Code of Conduct | DHPMCC">
  <section id="code-of-conduct" class="content-container policy-section">
    <header class="policy-header">
      <h1 class="page-title">DHPMCC Code of Conduct</h1>
      <p class="page-subtitle"><em>Last Updated: September 2026</em></p>
    </header>

    <div class="policy-preamble">
      <p>
        The Daniel H. Plotnick Memorial Computing Competition (DHPMCC) is committed to providing a safe, respectful, inclusive, and academically honest environment for all participants, volunteers, organizers, coaches, teachers, and guests.
      </p>
      <p>
        Participation in DHPMCC is a privilege. Everyone attending or participating in the competition is expected to conduct themselves responsibly and respectfully.
      </p>
    </div>

    <nav class="policy-toc" aria-label="Table of Contents">
      <span class="toc-label">Jump to section:</span>
      <ul class="toc-list">
        <li><a href="#respect">1. Respectful Conduct</a></li>
        <li><a href="#integrity">2. Academic &amp; Competitive Integrity</a></li>
        <li><a href="#technology">3. Technology &amp; Network Use</a></li>
        <li><a href="#school-policies">4. School &amp; Event Policies</a></li>
        <li><a href="#safety">5. Safety &amp; Property</a></li>
        <li><a href="#publicity">6. Photography, Recording &amp; Publicity</a></li>
        <li><a href="#reporting">7. Reporting Concerns</a></li>
        <li><a href="#enforcement">8. Enforcement</a></li>
        <li><a href="#scope">9. Scope</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="policy-body">
      <section id="respect" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">1. Respectful Conduct</h2>
        <p>Participants and attendees must:</p>
        <ul class="policy-list">
          <li>Treat other participants, organizers, volunteers, teachers, and guests with respect.</li>
          <li>Follow reasonable instructions from DHPMCC organizers, BCA personnel, and event staff.</li>
          <li>Refrain from harassment, bullying, threats, intimidation, discrimination, or other conduct that creates an unsafe or hostile environment.</li>
          <li>Respect school property, event facilities, equipment, and the property of others.</li>
          <li>Use appropriate language and behavior while participating in or attending the competition.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Harassment or discrimination based on characteristics protected by applicable law or school policy is not permitted.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="integrity" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">2. Academic and Competitive Integrity</h2>
        <p>Participants are expected to compete honestly.</p>
        <p>
          The DHPMCC Competition Rules establish the specific requirements governing submissions, collaboration, prohibited assistance, external resources, and other forms of competitive conduct. Conduct intended to gain an unfair advantage, interfere with another participant’s competition, or undermine the integrity of the contest may result in penalties or disqualification.
        </p>
        <p>Participants must not:</p>
        <ul class="policy-list">
          <li>Impersonate another participant.</li>
          <li>Access another participant’s account, submission, or private information.</li>
          <li>Attempt to compromise, disrupt, or interfere with DHPMCC systems or infrastructure.</li>
          <li>Intentionally interfere with another participant’s ability to compete.</li>
          <li>Misrepresent information to organizers or judges.</li>
          <li>Circumvent technical or administrative safeguards.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="technology" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">3. Technology and Network Use</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC-provided systems and networks may be used only for legitimate competition and event purposes.</p>
        <p>Participants may not intentionally:</p>
        <ul class="policy-list">
          <li>Attempt unauthorized access to systems, accounts, databases, or network resources.</li>
          <li>Deploy malicious software or code.</li>
          <li>Conduct denial-of-service attacks or other disruptive activity.</li>
          <li>Probe or exploit systems unrelated to the competition.</li>
          <li>Access, modify, or delete information belonging to another participant or the organizers.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Security vulnerabilities discovered unintentionally should be reported privately to the organizers rather than exploited or publicly disclosed during the competition.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="school-policies" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">4. School and Event Policies</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC may be held on the campus of Bergen County Academies (BCA). All participants and guests must comply with applicable BCA and Bergen County Technical Schools policies while on school property.</p>
        <p>Where a BCA or Bergen County Technical Schools policy imposes requirements beyond this Code of Conduct, the applicable school or district policy remains controlling.</p>
        <p>DHPMCC does not replace or supersede the rules, policies, disciplinary procedures, or authority of BCA or Bergen County Technical Schools.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="safety" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">5. Safety and Property</h2>
        <p>Participants must follow applicable safety instructions and must not engage in conduct that could reasonably endanger themselves or others.</p>
        <p>Damage, theft, unauthorized removal, or intentional misuse of school, DHPMCC, or another person’s property is prohibited.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="publicity" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">6. Photography, Recording, and Publicity</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC or authorized event personnel may photograph or record portions of the event for legitimate event, educational, archival, or promotional purposes, subject to applicable BCA policies and required permissions.</p>
        <p>DHPMCC will not knowingly publish a participant’s personal information beyond what is permitted by applicable policy, consent, or law.</p>
        <p>Participants should direct questions or concerns regarding photographs, recordings, or publicity to the DHPMCC organizers.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="reporting" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">7. Reporting Concerns</h2>
        <p>Anyone who experiences or witnesses conduct that may violate this Code of Conduct should report it to a DHPMCC organizer or an appropriate BCA staff member as soon as reasonably possible.</p>
        <p>Reports should be made in good faith. Retaliation against a person who makes a good-faith report or assists with an investigation is not permitted.</p>
        <p>For matters involving immediate safety concerns, participants should notify an appropriate BCA staff member or other responsible adult immediately.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="enforcement" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">8. Enforcement</h2>
        <p>DHPMCC organizers may take reasonable action in response to violations of this Code of Conduct, including:</p>
        <ul class="policy-list">
          <li>Warnings or instructions to stop the conduct.</li>
          <li>Removal from an activity or event area.</li>
          <li>Disqualification from the competition.</li>
          <li>Removal from the event.</li>
          <li>Restriction or prohibition from future DHPMCC events.</li>
          <li>Referral of the matter to BCA or other appropriate authorities when necessary.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The appropriate response depends on the circumstances and severity of the conduct.</p>
        <p>Where conduct occurs on BCA property or involves BCA students or personnel, BCA and Bergen County Technical Schools may independently apply their own policies and procedures.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="scope" class="policy-block">
        <h2 class="policy-section-title">9. Scope</h2>
        <p>This Code of Conduct applies to DHPMCC participants, volunteers, organizers, coaches, teachers, guests, and other persons participating in or attending DHPMCC activities.</p>
        <p>By registering for or participating in DHPMCC, participants and their supervising adults acknowledge that they are expected to follow this Code of Conduct in addition to the DHPMCC Competition Rules and applicable BCA policies.</p>
        <div class="policy-notice">
          <p>DHPMCC may update this Code of Conduct when necessary. The version published on the DHPMCC website at the time of an event will generally govern that event, subject to applicable school and district requirements.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .policy-section {
    padding-top: 2rem;
    padding-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .policy-header {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .page-title {
    font-size: 1.9rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111111;
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem 0;
  }

  .page-subtitle {
    color: #555555;
    font-size: 1rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .policy-preamble {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #2d3748;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .policy-preamble p {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .policy-toc {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .toc-label {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #111111;
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }

  .toc-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1.25rem;
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .toc-list li {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .toc-list a {
    color: var(--color-link);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .toc-list a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    color: var(--color-link-hover);
  }

  .policy-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2.25rem;
  }

  .policy-block {
    scroll-margin-top: 5rem;
  }

  .policy-section-title {
    font-size: 1.28rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #111111;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem 0;
    padding-bottom: 0.35rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .policy-block p {
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #2d3748;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .policy-list {
    list-style-type: disc;
    padding-left: 1.4rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .policy-list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: #2d3748;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .policy-notice {
    background-color: var(--color-bg-subtle);
    border-left: 3px solid #8b0000;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.15rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #4a5568;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .policy-notice p {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
